    "behavioral_notes": [
      {
        "element": "website.get_current_website / website.website_domain",
        "observation": "Multi-website routing: get_current_website() resolves the active website by precedence (session force_website_id -> context website_id -> request domain match via _get_current_website_id -> first website fallback). website_domain() returns Domain('website_id','in',[False,*ids]) so every website-scoped query transparently mixes generic (website_id=False) and site-specific records. _get_cached_values() prefetches user_id/company_id/default_lang_id/homepage_url to serve frontend dispatch before the env is fully initialised. None of this domain/precedence logic is visible in metadata.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "ir.http._serve_page / website.page._get_response (QWeb rendering)",
        "observation": "Page rendering is dynamic: ir.http._serve_fallback -> _serve_page looks up website.page via _get_page_info (URL + website_domain, specific-website-first, case-insensitive), then website.page._get_response renders the linked ir.ui.view through request.render() (QWeb). website.page _inherits ir.ui.view (view_id) and arch is a related field on the view, so the page IS a thin URL/SEO wrapper over a QWeb template. Public GET responses are memoised in an ORM cache ('templates.cached_values') keyed on (website,lang,path,debug) with a 3600s TTL and csrf re-injection on cache hits. Pure runtime behaviour, invisible to metadata.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "ir.http._register_website_track -> website.visitor._handle_webpage_dispatch",
        "observation": "Visitor analytics side-effect: _post_dispatch hooks every 200 response; for tracked templates (and non-bot, tracking not disabled) it calls website.visitor._handle_webpage_dispatch, which _get_visitor_from_request(force_create=True) creates/updates a website.visitor and appends a website.track row (url + page_id). Timezone is derived from geoip and persisted via a FOR NO KEY UPDATE SKIP LOCKED SQL UPDATE to dodge concurrent-update errors. A page view thus silently writes visitor/track rows -- a cross-model effect not derivable from the schema.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "website.page.write / get_unique_path (URL & key uniqueness)",
        "observation": "Editing a page URL re-slugifies it, enforces per-website uniqueness via get_unique_path (suffixes -1,-2...), cascades the new URL to related website.menu records, syncs website.homepage_url, and clears the 'templates' registry cache. Renaming regenerates a unique view key. These automations couple website.page <-> website.menu <-> website and bust render caches -- behaviour metadata cannot show.",
        "source": "code-read"
      },
      {
        "element": "frontend (OWL/JS website builder)",
        "observation": "website is the prime example of metadata gap #3: ~350 JS files and 152 XML templates implement the in-browser drag-and-drop website builder (40 OWL components incl. Configurator, snippet/page dialogs, fullscreen editor), 40+ public.interactions.edit snippet behaviours, 20+ monkey-patches of editor/navbar/popover prototypes, and 22 asset bundles (website.assets_editor=26, web.assets_frontend=34, website.assets_wysiwyg=13). Almost the entire UX lives in client-side OWL/JS, entirely outside Python model metadata.",
        "source": "static"
      }
