  "classification": {
    "value_model": "network",
    "activity_class": "primary",
    "apqc_category": "3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services",
    "rationale": "website is a value network (Stabell & Fjeldstad mediating technology): it IS the platform/infrastructure that mediates between the organization and an open population of visitors, and between visitors and the published content/forms/other apps (shop, blog, event, livechat). Its value is mediating-and-infrastructure: routing requests to the right website (get_current_website), rendering pages (QWeb), connecting parties via forms/menus, and its worth grows with the number of participants (visitors, published pages, linked apps) -- the hallmark of a network, not a sequential transformation (chain) or a problem-solving cycle (shop). activity_class is primary because operating that mediating infrastructure -- provisioning the web presence and the request/render/track service itself -- is the core service the module delivers, not a back-office support function. apqc_category 3.0 Market and Sell is chosen over 6.0 Manage Customer Service because the platform's primary purpose is the public-facing market presence, content publishing, SEO and lead/visitor capture (demand-side marketing channel) rather than post-sale case handling; customer-service flows (livechat, helpdesk) are optional add-on modules, whereas marketing/web-presence is the module's reason to exist."
  },
